  Slug: tome
  DisplayName: Tome
  IconPath: icons/sundries/books/book-symbol-triangle-silver-purple.webp
  Description: 'Tome implements embody lost knowledge and otherworldly insights.
    While a weathered book is most common, tome implements can have as many different
    form factors as there are ways to store knowledge, from carved clay tablets to
    bundles of knotted cords. Tome implements are associated with the harrow suit
    of books and the astrological signs of the stargazer and the underworld dragon.
    Initiate Benefit @Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.oADE2kM43wpF7MT5 inline]
    Adept Benefit @Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.gR8ODlO6au0laXo4 inline]
    Intensify Vulnerability Your tome''s power not only reads a creature''s present
    but even records its future actions. When you use Intensify Vulnerability, roll
    a d20 and set the result aside. At any time until the start of your next turn,
    you can use the d20 result you set aside for an attack roll to Strike the target
    of your Exploit Vulnerability, instead of rolling a new d20; this is a fortune
    effect. Paragon Benefit @Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.IGv5wS17AAi0U87W
    inline]'
